3. COMMERCIAL AND MONETIZED USE

You may not create, distribute, operate, sell, license, host, or otherwise
commercialize a Monetized Fork under this License.

To commercialize a Monetized Fork, You must obtain a separate written
commercial license from the Licensor before monetization begins. Unless a
different percentage is expressly agreed in that written commercial license,
the commercial license requires payment to the Licensor of twenty-five percent
(25%) of Gross Revenue attributable to the Monetized Fork.

The 25% revenue share applies to every Monetized Fork and Derivative Work
based on or incorporating the Software, regardless of whether the fork is
renamed, substantially modified, bundled with other software, accessed through
an API, or offered as a hosted service.

No commercial rights are granted by merely publishing a fork, accepting
contributions, adding a notice, or offering the fork under a different
license. A commercial license may include different payment terms, reporting
requirements, territory, duration, support terms, warranties, or other
conditions only when signed or otherwise expressly accepted in writing by the
Licensor.

4. REVENUE REPORTING AND PAYMENT

Unless a separate written commercial license states otherwise:

a. You must notify the Licensor before launching or monetizing a Monetized
   Fork;
b. You must provide a good-faith quarterly report showing Gross Revenue and
   the calculation of the 25% share;
c. You must pay the applicable share within thirty (30) days after the end of
   each calendar quarter;
d. You must keep commercially reasonable records supporting the reports for
   at least three (3) years; and
e. The Licensor may, on reasonable notice and no more than once per calendar
   year, request an independent review of records relevant to the revenue
   calculation. If an underpayment of more than five percent (5%) is found,
   You must pay the shortfall and reasonable review costs.

Payment instructions, currency, tax treatment, and the final method of
allocating revenue must be specified in the separate commercial agreement.
Until that agreement is executed, You must not monetize the Software.

